<main class="guia-log" id="inicio">
<section class="portada solo">
<div class="envoltura">
<div>
<div class="eti">MTG Arena · Player.log</div>
<h1>Where is MTG Arena&#x27;s Player.log, and why is it empty?</h1>
<p class="sub">Arena writes its log to a file called <code>Player.log</code>. On a PC it is in <code class="ruta-copiable">C:\Users\&lt;your user&gt;\AppData\LocalLow\Wizards Of The Coast\MTGA\</code>. If the file exists but has no games in it, the cause is almost always the same: Arena only writes your match data when "Detailed Logs (Plugin Support)" is turned on. Turn it on, restart Arena, and play one game.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion" id="donde">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="cab-sec">
<div class="eti">Find it</div>
<h2>Where to find it</h2>
</div>
<ol class="pasos-reg">
<li><span>Open File Explorer.</span></li>
<li><span>Click the address bar, paste <code class="ruta-copiable">%appdata%\..\LocalLow\Wizards Of The Coast\MTGA</code> and press Enter.</span></li>
<li><span>You will see <code>Player.log</code>. <code>AppData</code> is a hidden folder, which is why browsing for it by hand fails.</span></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion franja" id="previo">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="cab-sec">
<div class="eti">Previous session</div>
<h2>What Player-prev.log is</h2>
</div>
<div class="mtgo-caja sola">
<p>Arena keeps your last session. When you close and reopen the game, the previous log is saved as <code>Player-prev.log</code> in the same folder. If you just restarted Arena and your game is missing from <code>Player.log</code>, look in <code>Player-prev.log</code>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion" id="vacio">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="cab-sec">
<div class="eti">Troubleshooting</div>
<h2>When Player.log is empty or has no games</h2>
</div>
<p>Check these in order:</p>
<ol class="pasos-reg">
<li><span><b><a href="/detailed-logs/">"Detailed Logs (Plugin Support)"</a> is on.</b> In Arena: Options › Account. Without it, the log has only basic technical output and none of the game data a tracker needs.</span></li>
<li><span><b>You restarted Arena after turning it on.</b> The setting applies on the next launch.</span></li>
<li><span><b>You played a game after restarting.</b> The file only fills as you play.</span></li>
<li><span><b>You are looking at the right folder.</b> There are other <code>.log</code> files inside the Arena install folder; the one that matters is <code>Player.log</code> in <code>LocalLow</code>, not those.</span></li>
</ol>
<p>If all four are right and the file is still empty, <a href="/#contacto">send us</a> the file and the date it was written. We&#x27;d rather look at it than guess.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion franja" id="que-hace">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="cab-sec">
<div class="eti">ManaLab</div>
<h2>What ManaLab does with it</h2>
</div>
<div class="mtgo-caja sola">
<p>ManaLab reads <code>Player.log</code> and Arena&#x27;s card database without modifying them. It does not read Arena&#x27;s memory and does not connect to Wizards&#x27; servers. <a href="/safety/">How to check it →</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion" id="preguntas">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="cab-sec"><div class="eti">FAQ</div><h2>Questions</h2></div>
<div class="preguntas">
<details open><summary>Is it safe to open Player.log?</summary>
<p>Yes. It&#x27;s a text file; opening or copying it changes nothing.</p></details>
<details open><summary>Where is the Magic Online log?</summary>
<p><a href="/magic-online/">Magic Online</a> writes <code>mtgo.log</code> with nothing to turn on.</p></details>
</div>
<p class="actualizado">Updated 20 November 2026 · ManaLab</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion franja" id="siguiente">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="apoyo uno">
<div>
<div class="eti">Next step</div>
<h2>Let ManaLab save your games</h2>
<p>ManaLab saves every match you play in MTG Arena and Magic Online on your PC and shows what works: your win rates by deck, by opponent and by matchup, your mulligans, your mistakes and your sideboard changes.</p>
<p>The app is free. Only the AI analysis is paid.</p>
